  "solution": {
    "text": "For this to be true <math><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">cos</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math> and <math><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">cos</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math><br />So, <math><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>n</mi><mi>π</mi></math>&nbsp;<br />Since <math><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>0,20</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo></math> <math><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi><mn>6</mn></math>"
